Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-05-01
Subject: Make compiler units use compiler-side cutils align helper
License: expat

Several parameter managers align signed compiler-internal stack sizes
without importing `cutils`.  Bare calls instead bind to
`System.Align(PtrUInt, PtrUInt)`, which treats its operands as addresses.
Import the compiler helper so these operations remain in their signed
integer domain.

Import `cutils` at the remaining call sites that use integer
`align(...)`:

  compiler/avr/cpupara.pas
  compiler/m68k/cpupara.pas
  compiler/powerpc/cpupara.pas
  compiler/powerpc64/cpupara.pas

The `compiler/owar.pas` `align` occurrences are method calls on archive
buffer objects, not calls to the integer helper, and are intentionally
left alone.

--- a/compiler/avr/cpupara.pas
+++ b/compiler/avr/cpupara.pas
@@ -54,7 +54,8 @@
     uses
        verbose,systems,
        rgobj,
-       defutil,symsym;
+       defutil,symsym,
+       cutils;
 
 
     function tavrparamanager.get_volatile_registers_int(calloption : tproccalloption):tcpuregisterset;
--- a/compiler/m68k/cpupara.pas
+++ b/compiler/m68k/cpupara.pas
@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@
        verbose,
        globals,
        systems,
-       cpuinfo,cgutils,
+       cpuinfo,cutils,cgutils,
        defutil;
 
     procedure tm68kparamanager.getintparaloc(calloption : tproccalloption; nr : longint;var cgpara : TCGPara);
--- a/compiler/powerpc/cpupara.pas
+++ b/compiler/powerpc/cpupara.pas
@@ -54,6 +54,7 @@
     uses
        verbose,systems,
        defutil,symtable,
+       cutils,
        procinfo,cpupi;
 
 
--- a/compiler/powerpc64/cpupara.pas
+++ b/compiler/powerpc64/cpupara.pas
@@ -63,6 +63,7 @@
 uses
   verbose, systems,
   defutil,
+  cutils,
   procinfo, cpupi;
 
 function tppcparamanager.get_volatile_registers_int(calloption:
@@ -523,4 +524,3 @@
 begin
   paramanager := tppcparamanager.create;
 end.
